# # /amrf/
#
# AMRF (AntiMicrobial Resistance Framework): a vocabulary to describe
# antimicrobial resistance prediction models and the processing steps that
# prepare their inputs, so that a framework can discover which models can be
# applied to a sample. Developed as part of Cocos:
# https://github.com/DEAL-US/Cocos
#
# The vocabulary, its terms and the SHACL shapes (https://w3id.org/amrf/shapes)
# redirect to the Cocos deployment, which serves an HTML page or RDF (Turtle,
# JSON-LD) depending on the Accept header. Version IRIs redirect to the
# archived release on Zenodo.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# María Quirós Quiroga
# mquiros1@us.es
# GitHub username: mquirosq
#
# Daniel Ayala Hernández
# dayala1@us.es
# GitHub username: dayala1
#
# Fernando Sola Espinosa
# fsola@us.es
# GitHub username: fersolesp

RewriteEngine on

# Version 0.1.0: the Turtle file for RDF clients, the Zenodo record otherwise
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/turtle|application/x-turtle [NC]
RewriteRule ^0\.1\.0$ https://zenodo.org/records/24083396/files/amrf.ttl [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^0\.1\.0$ https://zenodo.org/records/24083396 [R=303,L]

# The vocabulary, its terms and the shapes
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://gin.us.es/cocos/amrf/$1 [R=303,L]
